mode: "100644"
text: "# Hook Craft by Format\n\nThe same idea has to be hooked differently depending on where it appears. Each format imposes a\ncutoff and a set of channels. Match the mechanism to the format's constraints.\n\n> Cutoffs and specs shift; treat the principles as durable and re-verify exact numbers. See\n> `caption-writer/references/platforms.md` for current per-platform caption limits.\n\n---\n\n## Caption first line\n\n- **Cutoff:** one line before \"…more\" — ~125 chars on Instagram, ~140 on LinkedIn, even fewer on\n  Facebook (~80). The hook must land *inside* the cutoff; tension at character 200 doesn't exist.\n- **Channel:** text only.\n- **Craft:** front-load the gap; cut every warm-up word. No greeting, no \"Happy Monday,\" no\n  describing the image.\n- **Test:** read only the first line, truncated at the cutoff. Would a stranger tap \"…more\"?\n\n## Video — first 1–3 seconds (Reels, TikTok, Shorts)\n\n- **Cutoff:** ~1–3 seconds. The single highest-stakes window in social.\n- **Channels (all at once):** visual (first frame + motion), verbal (first spoken words),\n  on-screen text (the written hook).\n- **Craft:**\n  - **Must work muted** — the on-screen text + visual carry the hook for sound-off viewers.\n  - Open *in motion* or on a striking frame; no logo, no slow intro, no \"Hey guys.\"\n  - The first spoken sentence is a hook mechanism, not a greeting.\n  - Match the on-screen text to the spoken hook (reinforce, don't repeat verbatim).\n- **Deliver:** give the user the verbal line **and** the on-screen text **and** a note on the\n  opening visual.\n\n## Carousel cover (slide 1)\n\n- **Cutoff:** a glance. The cover *is* the hook; if it doesn't promise the swipe, slides 2–10\n  never get seen.\n- **Channel:** a few words + visual; must be legible at thumbnail size.\n- **Craft:** one idea, big and clear. Promise the payoff the carousel delivers (\"5 hooks that\n  actually work →\"). Avoid cramming; the cover sells the swipe, the slides do the work.\n\n## Thread opener (first post)\n\n- **Cutoff:** the first post (≤280 chars on X; the lead post on LinkedIn/Threads).\n- **Channel:** text (sometimes + media).\n- **Craft:** promise the thread's through-line and payoff so people commit to reading down.\n  Tease the destination without giving it away. A weak first post means the thread dies at post\n  one.\n\n## YouTube — title + thumbnail\n\n- **Channels:** title (text) + thumbnail (visual) working *together* — they should add up to\n  more than either alone, not repeat each other.\n- **Craft:** curiosity + clarity. The title sets a gap; the thumbnail is the visual hook (a\n  face/emotion, a striking image, minimal legible text). Avoid pure clickbait the video doesn't\n  deliver — retention is the real ranking signal.\n\n## Email — subject + preview\n\n- **Cutoff:** subject truncates on mobile (~30–40 chars visible); the preview text is a second\n  hook.\n- **Craft:** specificity or curiosity, short. Use the preview line to extend the subject's gap,\n  not waste it on \"view in browser.\" Don't overpromise — opens you burn don't come back.\n\n---\n\n## Format quick reference\n\n| Format | Cutoff | Channels | The hook's job |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Caption | ~125 ch (IG) | text | earn the \"…more\" tap |\n| Short video | 1–3 sec | visual + verbal + text | stop the thumb, muted |\n| Carousel cover | a glance | words + visual | promise the swipe |\n| Thread opener | first post | text | promise the thread |\n| YouTube | title + thumb | text + visual | earn the click, honestly |\n| Email | ~30–40 ch subject | subject + preview | earn the open |\n\nWhatever the format: open the gap, inside the cutoff, in the brand's voice, true to what\nfollows.\n"
